    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.12) as our premier offensive weapon, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against Fedde and a high stolen base probability due to a slow opposing delivery. Alongside him, **Christian Yelich** (73.14) earns a strong start; his projection benefits from an elite platoon edge against Ober and the potential for late-inning efficiency. While we are sacrificing raw base projection to face top-tier arms like Skenes, the sheer volume of high-efficiency spots in the order ensures we remain competitive despite the threat posed by elite pitching.\n\nThe most difficult decision on our bench was **Chase Meidroth** (46.83), who fell just shy of the active roster threshold. While **Chase Meidroth** offers reliable middle-infielder depth, the optimizer favored the high-floor versatility of **Hyeseong Kim** (61.33) and **Junior Caminero** (61.60), whose superior matchup against weaker pitching staffs ultimately pushed them into the starting nine. We remain cautious regarding **Dillon Dingler** (40.08), as his score is hampered by a tough draw against Gausman and unfavorable wind conditions. Furthermore, the lineup must monitor the status of **Trea Turner** (49.79) and **Kyle Schwarber** (48.24); facing Skenes remains our highest-risk variable today, and we will be looking for early-game adjustments if these anchors struggle to maintain their xwOBA standards against elite velocity.",
